From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:39:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: wireless: brcm,bcm4329-fmac: allow a
 restricted DMA pool

A PCIe Wi-Fi chip runs firmware that parses untrusted frames. Platforms
that confine the chip's DMA to one region (with an IOMMU-less firewall
such as the Google gs201 S2MPU) describe that region as a
restricted-dma-pool and point the device node at it, as is already done
for other PCIe Wi-Fi bindings.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml  | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml
index 38e9a0444..858963108 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml
@@ -125,6 +125,11 @@ properties:
       NVRAM. This would normally be filled in by the bootloader from platform
       configuration data.
 
+  memory-region:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: A restricted-dma-pool region that all DMA of a PCIe device
+      bounces through, for platforms that limit the device's DMA to it.
+
   clocks:
     items:
       - description: External Low Power Clock input (32.768KHz)
